{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CfgyPvx6Wp4PB4nF1WfFF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change is a clean, additive consolidation that matches the codebase's established conventions.\n\n- **Single source of truth is in the right unit.** `OwnerIdentity` sits alongside the existing normalisation helpers (`OwnerTelephone`, `OwnerEmail`, `OwnerHousehold`, `OwnerAddress`) in `rest.function.owner`, and its javadoc states the same \"centralised so X and Y cannot disagree\" rationale those siblings use. The derivation logic lives there, and both the guard and the mapper consume it rather than re-deriving — so there's no duplicated key logic.\n- **Guard / exception / handler / YAML follow the existing triplet pattern.** `CheckOwnerIdentityUnique`, `DuplicateIdentityException`, `DuplicateIdentityExceptionHandler`, and the escalation + POST pipeline YAML are renamed/rewired consistently with how the three former guards were structured; nothing is left half-migrated (the three old checks, two old exceptions, two old handlers, and two old escalation YAMLs are all removed).\n- **No catch-all forms.** `CheckOwnerIdentityUnique` has a single `service` method; `OwnerIdentity` exposes a focused `of(Owner)` / `key(...)` pair with thin private normalisers delegating to the existing helpers. The three-check pipeline collapses to one step, which is simpler, not a dumping ground.\n- **Dangling references cleaned up.** `OwnerHousehold` and `OwnerTelephone` javadocs were updated to drop the now-deleted guards and point at their remaining collaborators (`AssignHousehold`, `OwnerIdentity`), and `NormalizeOwnerEmail`'s \"runs before\" note was retargeted — so the cross-reference web stays accurate.\n\nOne thing I weighed and let stand: the `OwnerMapper` now reaches into the `rest.function.owner` package via a fully-qualified expression, a coupling it didn't previously have. Given the explicit \"single source of truth\" intent and that the only alternative would re-implement the key in the mapper layer, sharing the one public helper is the better trade-off and reads naturally here."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":20260,"cache_read_input_tokens":11894,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":20260},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d0e4a4e3-6c49-4737-92d3-bd7f4daddfd2","uuid":"b3b9aa1e-2f83-417a-a36e-7b477a97e0e8","timestamp":"2026-10-04T09:38:46.687Z","request_id":"req_011CfgyPvhUTgXQkwaPSzZ7x"}
